// ============================================================================
// DIAGNOSTIC: Third-Party Event Timestamp Field Discovery
// ============================================================================
// PURPOSE: Discover actual field names available for calculating ingestion latency
//
// CONTEXT:
// We need to calculate ingestion latency for third-party events (non-CrowdStrike)
// but don't know the exact field names used by different vendors.
//
// LOOKING FOR:
// - Original event generation timestamp (when the event was created by the source system)
// - LogScale ingestion timestamp (when LogScale received the event)
// - Any intermediate timestamps that might be relevant
//
// EXPECTED PATTERNS:
// - *time*, *Time*         - Generic timestamp fields
// - *created*, *Created*   - Event creation timestamps
// - *ingested*, *Ingested* - Ingestion timestamps
// - *generated*, *Generated* - Event generation timestamps
// - event.*                - Nested event fields (ECS format)
// - Ngsiem.*              - CrowdStrike NGSIEM-specific fields
//
// ============================================================================

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Query 1: Verify third-party events exist
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#event.kind=event
| test(#Vendor != "crowdstrike")
| count(as=total_third_party_events)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Query 2: Sample events with ALL timestamp-related fields
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#event.kind=event
| test(#Vendor != "crowdstrike")
| head(10)
| table([@timestamp, #Vendor, #repo, *time*, *Time*, *created*, *Created*, *ingested*, *Ingested*, *generated*, *Generated*, event.*, Ngsiem.*])

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Query 3: Show unique vendors for context
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#event.kind=event
| test(#Vendor != "crowdstrike")
| groupBy([#Vendor], function=count(as=event_count))
| sort(event_count, order=desc)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Query 4: Explore field names (discover what fields exist)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#event.kind=event
| test(#Vendor != "crowdstrike")
| head(1)
| $"@rawstring" := format("%s", field=*)

// ============================================================================
// USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:
// ============================================================================
// 1. Run Query 1 first to verify data exists
// 2. Run Query 2 to see actual timestamp fields
// 3. Run Query 3 to understand which vendors are present
// 4. Run Query 4 to see the complete list of available fields
//
// NEXT STEPS:
// Once we identify the correct timestamp fields, update the ingestion latency
// metric calculation in the main dashboard query.
// ============================================================================
